__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Session artifacts must NEVER be tracked here — this repo is PUBLIC.
# The session hooks write .log/ into whatever repo they believe the session
# belonged to. On 2026-09-03 a stale `cd` made them believe a private-workspace
# session belonged to this repo, and `git add -A` published a 111KB transcript to
# GitHub. The cwd bug is fixed (session-end.sh rule 4), but this is the layer that
# holds even if that fix ever regresses: a misidentified repo can still misfile a
# log here, it just can no longer publish one. Every other repo in this workflow
# already ignores these; the asymmetry was the whole exposure.
.log/
.curiosities/
